selection sort
==================
selection sort is a comparison based algortihm.selection sort repeatedly selects the minimum element from the unsorted array and swaps with the first element in the unsorted array.this process contiues until array becomes sorted.

code:
============
public class SelectionSort{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        int arr[]={5,3,1,10,2};
        selectionSort(arr);
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            System.out.print(arr[i]+" ");
        }
    }
    static void selectionSort(int arr[]){
        int n=arr.length;
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length-1;i++){
            int miniIndex=i;
            for(int j=i+1;j<arr.length;j++){
                if(arr[j]<arr[miniIndex]){
                    miniIndex=j;
                }
            }
            int temp=arr[i];
            arr[i]=arr[miniIndex];
            arr[miniIndex]=temp;
        } } }

TC:Avg ,best,worst case time complexity O(n^2)
SC:O(1)

BubbleSort
=====================
comparing adjacent elements repeatedly at each iteration largest element moves to correct position in end of the array is called bubble sort
code
===============
public class BubbleSort{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        int arr[]={5,1,3,2};
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<arr.length-i-1;j++){
                if(arr[j]>arr[j+1]){
                    int temp=arr[j];
                    arr[j]=arr[j+1];
                    arr[j+1]=temp;
                }
            }
        }
    for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
        System.out.print(arr[i]);
    }
    }
}
TC:O(n^2)
SC:O(1)

Insertion Sort
======================
pick one element and put into the current of the array
code:
===============
public class InsertionSort{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        int arr[]={20,5,3,4,1,10};
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            int j=i;
            while(j>0 && arr[j-1]>arr[j]){
                int temp=arr[j];
                arr[j]=arr[j-1];
                arr[j-1]=temp;
                j--;
            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            System.out.print(arr[i]+" ");
        }
    }
}
TC:worst case and averageO(n^2)
best case:O(n)

